 ## License
 
 MIT — see [LICENSE](LICENSE).
+
+
+## Private proposal: explicit human counterpart
+
+The optional `humans[].counterpart_persona` field names one existing actor ID.
+Omit it for an unbound human; explicit null, invalid IDs, missing actors and two
+humans bound to the same actor are rejected. Existing organizations without the
+field retain their previous human registry output. When mappings exist, the
+compiled human registry includes a `counterpart_persona` column.
+
+```yaml
+humans:
+  - id: board-member
+    name: Board Member
+    counterpart_persona: coordinator
+    email: member@example.org
+```
+
+This example assumes an actor named `coordinator` already exists. A counterpart
+is an organizational relationship, not evidence of channel authentication.
+Names, role labels and `reports_to_human` never infer it. An email address alone
+does not authorize a Telegram or PhantomChat session. Consumers must verify the
+native channel principal and derive applicable access from existing PhantomOrg
+policy; this field introduces no separate human grants, owner assignment or
+category-zero privilege. It does not change native collaborative memory or tools.
+This is a private compatibility proposal, not an installed upstream feature.
